  "note": "Annotation merge. The strict comparison is convex/lib/annotationMerge resolveUpsert, reused rather than reimplemented; this layer adds only the tie-break (device sequence, then device id) that an outbox draining several edits inside one millisecond needs. applyAnnotationMerge then re-attaches the server-owned fields the client never saw: a Readest push carries no voice fields, so a plain round-trip through an unmodified reader must not strip the audio off a voice note. A cross-profile id collision is invalid input, not a merge, for the same reason isSameOwner exists on the Convex side.",
